Error [E3203]: `Point` is not a C-compatible type for a foreign function parameter or return.
  --> tests/ui/cffi_e3203_struct_needs_layout_c.jet:6:38
    |
  6 |     fn make_point(x: Int, y: Int) -> Point = "demo_make_point";
    |                                      ^^^^^
 Why: `@Extern` / `@Bindgen` functions must use types with a stable C ABI at the edge.
 Fix: Use scalars, `String`, or a struct with C layout; pointers only through the gated tier.
